        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Ohhhh... *slaps head*\n\nI misread the documentation. I thought the described `function` placement was what I did in my first solution, I had not understood that it could also wrap the whole snippet. And I also missed that inline function loaders are not cached, I thought that would also only give me load-once granularity.\n\nThank you so much, it all works and is organized the way I prefer! Sorry for wasting your time.\n\nShould I open another issue (feature request) for callback-based transformations, or is that out of scope? It would provide a lot of possibilities, and not need an external regex engine.",
