            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Thank you so much, it all works and is organized the way I prefer! Sorry for wasting your time.\n\nNo worries! This is probably partially a convoluted documentation issue. The overall process is rather flexible, so it is hard to explicitly document everything. Some complex setups are sometimes even better to leave behind a little friction to get.\n\n> Should I open another issue (feature request) for callback-based transformations, or is that out of scope? It would provide a lot of possibilities, and not need an external regex engine.\n\nI don't think this is a good fit for 'mini.snippets'. It is already pretty complex and going down the rabbit hole of \"very flexible snippet engine\" will add even more. The current idea is that \"prepare step\" results in fully formed LSP specification snippets and that's it. Everything after that is how the LSP specification defines it.",
